---
title: AdviseCare - Sequence Diagram SD-31 - External Referral and Overdue Check
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor SWO as Student Welfare Officer
    participant W as Web App
    participant C as ExternalReferralsController
    participant S as ExternalReferralService
    participant BG as ExternalReferralOverdueService
    participant R as IGenericRepository
    participant DB as SQL Server
    SWO->>W: Refer student to "Example Bank" with follow-up date
    W->>C: POST /api/ExternalReferrals {caseId, externalServiceId, followUpDueAt}
    C->>S: CreateAsync(CreatorId, request)
    S->>R: Case open and accepted by this officer, service active
    S->>R: CreateAsync(referral, status = sent, isOverdue = false)
    R->>DB: INSERT EXTERNALREFERRALS
    loop periodically (hosted background service)
        BG->>R: Referrals with status sent and followUpDueAt in the past
        BG->>R: Set isOverdue = true, SaveAsync()
        R->>DB: UPDATE EXTERNALREFERRALS
    end
    SWO->>W: Log follow-up outcome
    W->>C: PUT /api/ExternalReferrals/{id} {followUpOutcome}
    C->>S: UpdateAsync(ExternalReferralId, request)
    S->>R: UpdateAsync(status = followedUp, isOverdue = false)
    SWO->>W: Close referral
    W->>C: PUT /api/ExternalReferrals/{id}/close
    C->>S: CloseAsync(ExternalReferralId)
    S->>R: UpdateAsync(status = closed)
    R->>DB: UPDATE EXTERNALREFERRALS
    C-->>W: 200 OK
